&lt;/span>
&lt;/h2>&lt;p>忆往昔峥嵘岁月：&lt;/p>
&lt;ul>
&lt;li>开始健身。和好兄弟们吃了n次海鲜自助。&lt;/li>
&lt;li>在n次尝试后，拿下雅思。😂&lt;/li>
&lt;li>挖到数个网络协议漏洞。&lt;/li>
&lt;li>瓦洛兰特上钻石。&lt;/li>
&lt;li>今年成功答辩，完成了一份我自我满意的毕业设计。也标志着本科期间在网络领域研究的结束。&lt;/li>
&lt;li>拿到北欧offer。&lt;/li>
&lt;li>带队字节AI安全比赛🥉。&lt;/li>
&lt;li>Datacon大数据安全挑战赛AI安全赛道🥉。&lt;/li>
&lt;li>完成 Blackhat Aisa投稿。&lt;/li>
&lt;li>全国旅游。南京 -&amp;gt; 成都 -&amp;gt; 九寨沟 -&amp;gt; 大理 -&amp;gt; 丽江 -&amp;gt; 陕西。&lt;/li>
&lt;li>人生第一次徒步 &amp;ndash; 虎跳峡。并爱上了徒步。徒步中收获很多友谊。&lt;/li>
&lt;li>拿到北欧5年签证。&lt;/li>
&lt;li>入手人生第一台相机A7C2。&lt;/li>
&lt;li>软件所实习年数+1&lt;/li>
&lt;/ul>
&lt;p>折戟沙场：&lt;/p>
&lt;ul>
&lt;li>未能找到女朋友😭&lt;/li>
&lt;li>FUZZ论文还是没写出来 555😭&lt;/li>
&lt;/ul>
&lt;p>展望未来：&lt;/p>
&lt;ul>
&lt;li>找个岗位制博士读读。&lt;/li>
&lt;li>去北欧徒步，去看最好的风景。&lt;/li>
&lt;li>收获更多友谊。&lt;/li>
&lt;li>技术上能有更大突破。&lt;/li>
&lt;li>遇见最好的她。&lt;/li>
&lt;/ul>
&lt;p>江湖，是少年人的江湖。
希望我未来可以，攀更高的山峰，看更美的风景，遇见更优秀的她，哈哈哈，快哉快哉。&lt;/p></description></item><item><title>runrunzi的2023年终总结</title><link>https://BestRun.github.io/life/2023_summary/</link><pubDate>Sun, 31 Dec 2023 15:48:06 +0800</pubDate><guid>https://BestRun.github.io/life/2023_summary/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="前言" >前言
&lt;span>
&lt;a href="#%e5%89%8d%e8%a8%80">
&lt;svg viewBox="0 0 28 23" height="100%" width="19" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">&lt;path d="M10 13a5 5 0 0 0 7.54.54l3-3a5 5 0 0 0-7.07-7.07l-1.72 1.71" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-miterlimit="10" stroke-width="2"/>&lt;path d="M14 11a5 5 0 0 0-7.54-.54l-3 3a5 5 0 0 0 7.07 7.07l1.71-1.71" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-miterlimit="10" stroke-width="2"/>&lt;/svg>
&lt;/a>
&lt;/span>
&lt;/h2>&lt;p>只有时常回过头看走过的路，才能更好的迈向远方。 &amp;ndash; runrunzi
不知不觉一年又过去了，此时的我一个人坐在电脑前，孤零零地写着年终总结，（😭原来大家跨年都有人陪，只有我还是一个人。
不是很想写流水账，就分成几个模块来写吧。想了想，打算这么分&lt;/p>
&lt;ul>
&lt;li>总的来说&lt;/li>
&lt;li>工作&amp;amp;技术&lt;/li>
&lt;li>生活&lt;/li>
&lt;li>展望&amp;amp;规划&lt;/li>
&lt;/ul>
&lt;h3 id="总的来说" >总的来说
&lt;span>
&lt;a href="#%e6%80%bb%e7%9a%84%e6%9d%a5%e8%af%b4">
&lt;svg viewBox="0 0 28 23" height="100%" width="19" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">&lt;path d="M10 13a5 5 0 0 0 7.54.54l3-3a5 5 0 0 0-7.07-7.07l-1.72 1.71" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-miterlimit="10" stroke-width="2"/>&lt;path d="M14 11a5 5 0 0 0-7.54-.54l-3 3a5 5 0 0 0 7.07 7.07l1.71-1.71" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-miterlimit="10" stroke-width="2"/>&lt;/svg>
&lt;/a>
&lt;/span>
&lt;/h3>&lt;p>今年是我人生中很关键的一年，这一年会大致决定我未来的去向，未来到底要做什么。我的步调可以说是一半学，一半摆。身边的朋友有的去USA读PHD，有的去阿里这种大厂追梦，而我也在犹豫中慢慢向前摸索自己未来的路。&lt;/p>
&lt;p>一年一瞬间就过去了，可能未来大概率是要去继续出国读个书的。今年最大的收获可能就是明白没有简单的路吧，体验了工业界和学术界后，有了些感觉，这些写在下面的段落中。&lt;/p>
&lt;h3 id="工作技术" >工作&amp;amp;技术
&lt;span>
&lt;a href="#%e5%b7%a5%e4%bd%9c%e6%8a%80%e6%9c%af">
&lt;svg viewBox="0 0 28 23" height="100%" width="19" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">&lt;path d="M10 13a5 5 0 0 0 7.54.54l3-3a5 5 0 0 0-7.07-7.07l-1.72 1.71" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-miterlimit="10" stroke-width="2"/>&lt;path d="M14 11a5 5 0 0 0-7.54-.54l-3 3a5 5 0 0 0 7.07 7.07l1.71-1.71" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-miterlimit="10" stroke-width="2"/>&lt;/svg>
&lt;/a>
&lt;/span>
&lt;/h3>&lt;p>今年的开始是从一份实习开始的，我十分感谢这份实习，在这次实习中我学到了很多东西，体会到了前阿里云顶级sec团队的工作氛围（吹就完了）。&lt;/p>
&lt;h4 id="工作" >工作
&lt;span>
&lt;a href="#%e5%b7%a5%e4%bd%9c">
&lt;svg viewBox="0 0 28 23" height="100%" width="19" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">&lt;path d="M10 13a5 5 0 0 0 7.54.54l3-3a5 5 0 0 0-7.07-7.07l-1.72 1.71" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-miterlimit="10" stroke-width="2"/>&lt;path d="M14 11a5 5 0 0 0-7.54-.54l-3 3a5 5 0 0 0 7.07 7.07l1.71-1.71" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-miterlimit="10" stroke-width="2"/>&lt;/svg>
&lt;/a>
&lt;/span>
&lt;/h4>&lt;h5 id="eagle-cloud-internship" >Eagle Cloud Internship
&lt;span>
&lt;a href="#eagle-cloud-internship">
&lt;svg viewBox="0 0 28 23" height="100%" width="19" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">&lt;path d="M10 13a5 5 0 0 0 7.54.54l3-3a5 5 0 0 0-7.07-7.07l-1.72 1.71" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-miterlimit="10" stroke-width="2"/>&lt;path d="M14 11a5 5 0 0 0-7.54-.54l-3 3a5 5 0 0 0 7.07 7.07l1.71-1.71" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-miterlimit="10" stroke-width="2"/>&lt;/svg>
&lt;/a>
&lt;/span>
&lt;/h5>&lt;p>今年过年面试了亿格云公司，感谢Y4👴的推荐，直接把我推到了叶总面前。面我的是刘师傅（诸多src前几名，传闻俩月挖洞挖了辆宝马）这次面试回想起来，我只想用灾难二字形容。&lt;/p>
&lt;ul>
&lt;li>简单说几个NLP相关算法，（🤔️&lt;/li>
&lt;li>简单说一次你的渗透经历，（🤔️&lt;/li>
&lt;li>等等等等，我只会&amp;ndash;🤔️
可能是我是短期实习，感谢贵司还是给了我实习的机会。
在这里呆了俩月，学到了很多业务上的能力，也明白了一些事情：&lt;/li>
&lt;li>功能上线前不可能总让你完全准备好，先做起来。&lt;/li>
&lt;li>很多业务是你根本没接触过的，这时候就需要你快速学习的能力。
实习了两个月，我感觉自己还是更向往学术界一些，工业界可能对我这种不安分的人来说有点boring，加上学校一堆课，就回到了学校。&lt;/li>
&lt;/ul>
&lt;h5 id="iscas-intership" >ISCAS Intership
&lt;span>
&lt;a href="#iscas-intership">
&lt;svg viewBox="0 0 28 23" height="100%" width="19" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">&lt;path d="M10 13a5 5 0 0 0 7.54.54l3-3a5 5 0 0 0-7.07-7.07l-1.72 1.71" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-miterlimit="10" stroke-width="2"/>&lt;path d="M14 11a5 5 0 0 0-7.54-.54l-3 3a5 5 0 0 0 7.07 7.07l1.71-1.71" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-miterlimit="10" stroke-width="2"/>&lt;/svg>
&lt;/a>
&lt;/span>
&lt;/h5>&lt;p>回到学校，就立刻进入到了找暑期实习的状态。三月到五月面了一堆公司，这里挂一下当时的emo推。
&lt;img src="https://BestRun.github.io/pictures/20231231162233.png" width="600" height="800">&lt;/p>
&lt;p>五月份投了ISCAS的系统安全实习生，没想到顺利的通过了之后就开启了直到今天的“科研”实习。&lt;/p>
&lt;p>可以说，这段实习让我对安全，科研都有了新的认知。&lt;/p>
&lt;p>七月份到十月份，疯狂的读了很多fuzz相关的论文，感觉打开了新世界（以前甚至肤浅的觉得sec的科研有点花拳绣腿的感觉，不是很实用）。现在发现，学术界才是引领sec发展的最前线。&lt;/p>
&lt;p>感谢导让我自己负责一个项目，一直坐到今天，也快有了结果。&lt;/p>
&lt;h4 id="技术" >技术
&lt;span>
&lt;a href="#%e6%8a%80%e6%9c%af">
&lt;svg viewBox="0 0 28 23" height="100%" width="19" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">&lt;path d="M10 13a5 5 0 0 0 7.54.54l3-3a5 5 0 0 0-7.07-7.07l-1.72 1.71" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-miterlimit="10" stroke-width="2"/>&lt;path d="M14 11a5 5 0 0 0-7.54-.54l-3 3a5 5 0 0 0 7.07 7.07l1.71-1.71" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-miterlimit="10" stroke-width="2"/>&lt;/svg>
&lt;/a>
&lt;/span>
&lt;/h4>&lt;p>今年技术感觉没啥大的进步，但由于GPT的出现，加上学校里的成，我更深入地去了解了一些NLP的相关知识，也去实践了一些AI和安全相关的东西。最大的进步还是入坑了FUZZ领域吧，还是要继续加油啊，小Hao！&lt;/p>
&lt;p>此外还被西北大学的xing教授拉去帮忙AIXCC比赛，希望以后有机会去USA读个PHD。&lt;/p>
&lt;h3 id="生活情感" >生活（情感）
&lt;span>
&lt;a href="#%e7%94%9f%e6%b4%bb%e6%83%85%e6%84%9f">
&lt;svg viewBox="0 0 28 23" height="100%" width="19" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">&lt;path d="M10 13a5 5 0 0 0 7.54.54l3-3a5 5 0 0 0-7.07-7.07l-1.72 1.71" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-miterlimit="10" stroke-width="2"/>&lt;path d="M14 11a5 5 0 0 0-7.54-.54l-3 3a5 5 0 0 0 7.07 7.07l1.71-1.71" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-miterlimit="10" stroke-width="2"/>&lt;/svg>
&lt;/a>
&lt;/span>
&lt;/h3>&lt;p>今年的生活可以说是有滋有味了，从小Hao的qq空间可以看出来。&lt;/p>
&lt;p>此外，今年最大的突破可以说是开始了健身。自己的身体摆了两年，今年终于开始要健身了，目前已经健身了一个月，自我感觉良好，从刚开始10kg的哑铃都做不动到现在可以挑战17.5kg，进步还是肉眼可见的哈。&lt;/p>
&lt;p>&lt;strong>情感方面，本人目前单身，欢迎来打扰o.o&lt;/strong>&lt;/p>
&lt;h3 id="展望规划" >展望&amp;amp;规划
&lt;span>
&lt;a href="#%e5%b1%95%e6%9c%9b%e8%a7%84%e5%88%92">
&lt;svg viewBox="0 0 28 23" height="100%" width="19" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">&lt;path d="M10 13a5 5 0 0 0 7.54.54l3-3a5 5 0 0 0-7.07-7.07l-1.72 1.71" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-miterlimit="10" stroke-width="2"/>&lt;path d="M14 11a5 5 0 0 0-7.54-.54l-3 3a5 5 0 0 0 7.07 7.07l1.71-1.71" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-miterlimit="10" stroke-width="2"/>&lt;/svg>
&lt;/a>
&lt;/span>
&lt;/h3>&lt;p>关于留学：申请ing，没啥好说的&lt;/p>
&lt;p>我是想读个master当gap year然后考虑下去学术界还是工业界。如果没有合适的奥佛，我就打算做一年科研助理直接去学术界了，毕竟master对读博也没啥大用。&lt;/p>
&lt;p>前两天和梁兄（一位在USA追梦的PHD）交流了一下，我跟他说，我萌生了Gap Year的想法，他也是很支持。他也赞同，花点时间搞清楚自己想要什么更加重要。&lt;/p>
&lt;p>之前和西北大学的某位前辈请教，问他关于读博的问题，他告所我说sec的PHD还是更看技术一些吧，gpa不要太低就好，说我可以直接申。但是今年是来不及辣，看明年咯，希望一些顺利！&lt;/p></description></item><item><title>A diary in a special time</title><link>https://BestRun.github.io/life/a-simple-diary/</link><pubDate>Sat, 21 Oct 2023 11:15:13 +0800</pubDate><guid>https://BestRun.github.io/life/a-simple-diary/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="my-life-and-mental-state" >My life and mental state
&lt;span>
&lt;a href="#my-life-and-mental-state">
&lt;svg viewBox="0 0 28 23" height="100%" width="19" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">&lt;path d="M10 13a5 5 0 0 0 7.54.54l3-3a5 5 0 0 0-7.07-7.07l-1.72 1.71" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-miterlimit="10" stroke-width="2"/>&lt;path d="M14 11a5 5 0 0 0-7.54-.54l-3 3a5 5 0 0 0 7.07 7.07l1.71-1.71" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-miterlimit="10" stroke-width="2"/>&lt;/svg>
&lt;/a>
&lt;/span>
&lt;/h2>&lt;p>Today is Saturday, and I don&amp;rsquo;t want to overwhelm myself with work, even though I&amp;rsquo;m facing the most intense pressure I&amp;rsquo;ve ever experienced in my undergraduate years as I strive to secure a Master&amp;rsquo;s or PhD position.&lt;/p>
&lt;p>Just yesterday, I gave a presentation for one of my courses. The teacher, an associate professor from Canada, transformed the presentation into a meaningful conversation. He offered a piece of advice that has left a lasting impact on me and provided valuable lessons. He emphasized the importance of always being prepared for a presentation and understanding the purpose at any given time. This advice is especially crucial when you&amp;rsquo;re planning to study abroad, as it&amp;rsquo;s easy to feel lost in a new environment. He humorously added, &amp;ldquo;In many years, you might forget my name and the name of the course, but you&amp;rsquo;ll remember being in a strange place, with an strange course and teacher, telling you to always be prepared and know your purpose.&amp;rdquo;&lt;/p>
&lt;p>His words deeply resonated with me. Lately, I&amp;rsquo;ve been juggling various commitments, such as internships, preparing for the IELTS, and applying for Master&amp;rsquo;s programs. It&amp;rsquo;s been three months since I last wrote a blog or reflected on my life and studies.So today, I took a moment to sit down in my lab and write this blog to summarize the past few months of my work and life.&lt;/p>
&lt;p>I&amp;rsquo;d like to share what I&amp;rsquo;ve been up to recently. Firstly, I&amp;rsquo;m still engrossed in my internship project focused on fuzzing at ISCAS. What&amp;rsquo;s more, I&amp;rsquo;m about to commence work with Professor Xing on the AIxCC competition, and I&amp;rsquo;m faced with three course projects that I must complete – it feels like quite a workload!&lt;/p>
&lt;p>Additionally, this week I&amp;rsquo;ve prepared all the application materials for my UK university applications. I&amp;rsquo;m set to apply to the University of Southampton next Monday.&lt;/p>
&lt;p>Furthermore, I&amp;rsquo;m in the process of deciding the direction for my bachelor&amp;rsquo;s thesis. I can use the progress I made in AIxCC competition as my bachelor&amp;rsquo;s thesis, but my school tutor also give my a direction about detecting encrypted malicious traffic.&lt;/p>
&lt;p>On top of all this, my IELTS score currently stands at only 6. I need to put in the effort to improve it to 6.5 by the end of this year. And, I also have to obtain a GRE score this year! The NUS need GRE grade, cry!&lt;/p>
&lt;p>Yes, there are just too many tasks on my plate.&lt;/p>
&lt;p>Despite my initial intention to avoid discussing anything related to computer knowledge formally, I&amp;rsquo;ve found it difficult to do so. First, let me list all the tasks I need to complete:&lt;/p>
&lt;ul>
&lt;li>Course projects
&lt;ul>
&lt;li>NLP course&lt;/li>
&lt;li>CV course&lt;/li>
&lt;li>AI Reach Practice&lt;/li>
&lt;/ul>
&lt;/li>
&lt;li>Internship project&lt;/li>
&lt;li>IELTS&lt;/li>
&lt;li>GRE&lt;/li>
&lt;li>AIxCC competition&lt;/li>
&lt;li>School applications (Personal Statement, Reference Letter, and so on&amp;hellip;)&lt;/li>
&lt;/ul>
&lt;p>However, I want to make it clear that I&amp;rsquo;m not writing this blog to complain. My aim is to tackle these challenges one by one.&lt;/p>
&lt;h2 id="some-research-experiences" >Some Research experiences
&lt;span>
&lt;a href="#some-research-experiences">
&lt;svg viewBox="0 0 28 23" height="100%" width="19" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">&lt;path d="M10 13a5 5 0 0 0 7.54.54l3-3a5 5 0 0 0-7.07-7.07l-1.72 1.71" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-miterlimit="10" stroke-width="2"/>&lt;path d="M14 11a5 5 0 0 0-7.54-.54l-3 3a5 5 0 0 0 7.07 7.07l1.71-1.71" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-miterlimit="10" stroke-width="2"/>&lt;/svg>
&lt;/a>
&lt;/span>
&lt;/h2>&lt;p>After that, I want to share some research experiences I&amp;rsquo;ve faced in the last few months. Perhaps I should list them for a clearer expression.&lt;/p>
&lt;ol>
&lt;li>You should divide your tasks into smaller, more manageable ones until you can.&lt;/li>
&lt;li>Many times, you may think you&amp;rsquo;ve found a paper that could solve your problems, but most of the time, you&amp;rsquo;ll find it couldn&amp;rsquo;t after some experimentation. This is a common occurrence, so keep on reading and trying.&lt;/li>
&lt;li>Writing a weekly summary, in my internship, it is called a &amp;ldquo;weekly report,&amp;rdquo; can make your project clearer, and perhaps you will get new ideas when you write it.&lt;/li>
&lt;li>Don&amp;rsquo;t always think you should wait until you are well-prepared to start. When you&amp;rsquo;re confused, what you should do is start. You can do five or more tasks, even if they are not well-prepared, instead of one task for which you&amp;rsquo;ve prepared everything well.&lt;/li>
&lt;/ol>
&lt;p>Hope everything goes smoothly afterwards!&lt;/p></description></item></channel></rss>